      "body": "## Motivation\n\ntest/registered/cpu/test_subblock_sparse_attention.py has been disabled with `disabled=\"Xeon import initializes CUDA-only vsa (#43334); until 2026-10-24\"`. That deadline has passed, and the import no longer initializes CUDA-only state — `from sglang.multimodal_gen.runtime.platforms.cuda import _SubBlockSparseAttentionBackendResolver` imports cleanly on a CPU-only box on current main.\n\nWhile the test sat disabled it also drifted: `MiniMaxH3PipelineConfig.validate_server_args` now reads `server_args.performance_mode`, which the fixtures' SimpleNamespace never set, so 7 of the 31 tests raised AttributeError as soon as anything ran them. This fixes the fixtures and removes the expired marker so the Xeon suite (`stage-a-test-cpu-intel`) picks the test back up.\n\n## Modifications\n\n- Removed the expired `disabled=` argument from `register_cpu_ci`.\n- Added `performance_mode=\"speed\"` to the two `SimpleNamespace` server_args fixtures that `validate_server_args` reads.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\n`pytest test/registered/cpu/test_subblock_sparse_attention.py` — 31 passed, 7 subtests passed, on a CPU-only box against current main. ruff format and the pre-commit ruff selection are clean.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Format your code according to the [Code Formatting with Pre-Commit](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#code-formatting-with-pre-commit).\n- [x] Add unit tests as outlined in the [Run and add unit tests](https://docs.sglang.io/developer_guide/contribution_guide.html#run-and-add-unit-tests). (this PR re-enables one)\n- [x] Update documentation / docstrings / example tutorials as needed — not needed.\n- [ ] Provide throughput / latency benchmark results and accuracy evaluation results as needed — not applicable for a test re-enable.\n\n<!-- pr-states:start -->\n---\n### CI States\n\nLatest PR Test (Base): <!-- slot:pr-test:start -->:x: [Run #40623388755](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623388755)<!-- slot:pr-test:end -->\nLatest PR Test (Extra): <!-- slot:pr-test-extra:start -->:x: [Run #40623388682](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623388682)<!-- slot:pr-test-extra:end -->\nLatest PR Test (AMD ROCm 10): <!-- slot:pr-test-amd:start -->:x: [Run #40623388646](https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/actions/runs/40623388646)<!-- slot:pr-test-amd:end -->\n\n> [!TIP]\n> Base CI only covers the core cases, and its workload may not exercise your change. Use `/rerun-test` to run the tests your change touches, or copy this prompt for an agent:\n>\n> ```text\n> Find the registered tests this PR affects and run them with /rerun-test, following https://github.com/sgl-project/sglang/blob/main/.agents/skills/rerun-test/SKILL.md\n> ```\n<!-- pr-states:end -->",
